+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today they are turned away because rentals can only be whole days. Renting by the hour lets the school serve them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: a non-negative integer number of euro cents for one hour of rental.
+- `quote` and `book` accept a sub-day period that starts and ends on the hour (UTC). Its total is `hourlyPrice` × number of hours.
+- An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be quoted or booked by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw.
+- Whole-day periods and their pricing are unchanged. Hourly bookings take part in the existing no-overlap rule, so an hourly rental blocks a whole-day one and vice versa.
+- Assumptions (recorded in the spec): "shorter than a day" means strictly less than 24 hours and at least 1 hour; an hourly period may cross midnight UTC; the long-stay discount never applies (it needs 3 or more days).
+- Out of scope: part-hour periods, hourly periods of 24 hours or more, a daily-price cap for long hourly rentals, availability queries by hour, cancellation.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: equipment gains an optional `hourlyPrice`, and periods may be sub-day on-the-hour periods. It is expressed as added requirements because `rentals` is still being introduced by the unarchived change `add-rental-service`; the new period requirement makes an explicit exception to that change's whole-day period rule.
+
+## Impact
+
+Depends on `add-rental-service` (the service, `src/rental.ts`, period parsing and pricing do not exist yet), which must be implemented first. Interacts with `add-long-stay-discount` (not applicable below 3 days) and `add-rental-availability` (whole-day queries must see hourly bookings through the shared overlap check). Touches `src/rental.ts` and `src/rental.test.ts`; no dependencies added.
